<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2782"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 6:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Please go to this collection of VERY strange letters and please tell me if you see any connection to the BTK case. <BR>In som of the pages there is refered to &#34;the monster&#34; and also in some of them people are toruered to death. <BR> <BR><a href="http://images.google.dk/images?q=bdmonkeys/notebook&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;start=0&amp;sa=N&amp;filter=0" target=_top>http://images.google.dk/images?q=bdmonkeys/noteboo k&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;start=0&amp;sa=N&amp;filter=0</a> <BR>When you see the pics of the letters. klick on the image of the letter. Then when it shows a small pic of the letter page, klick on the image of the letter. Then it will show first in an enlarged version, but soon get back to a smaller verion. Then move your curser over the lower left corner of the letter and there will show a symbol that make it possible to enlrge the letter, klick on that symbol, and then you can read everything that is in tyhe letter. <BR> <BR>I found thise letters while resarching for the word  garote, a word that was provided in one of BTK´s letters. <BR> <BR>Also if you go to <a href="http://www.google.com" target=_top>www.google.com</a> and write in <BR>garote.bdmonkeys.net, this is the web where the strange letters are from. The problem is that it is impossible to get into that website. <BR> <BR>If anyone of you find out how to enter that web, please let me know. <BR> <BR>skov <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2782-->
<!--Post: 2792--><!--Time: 1104133004-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2792"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 11:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Skov, <BR> <BR>Glad to make your acquaintance.  I&#39;ve enjoyed your posts. <BR> <BR>These look like a mixture of school notes and video game play/design notes.  Very much like the ones my teenage son and his friends make.  They are into game creation, so their game cheat and crib writings take on an ominously realistic tone about fantasy stuff, mixed with geometry, trigonometry, graphics, and other unlikely things.  At least, that&#39;s what it looks like to me. <BR> <BR>Probably a false alarm, but keep up the good work.  I agree there is a worthwhile chance that we will find BTK to have left tracks somewhere on the web.  Some of your other avenues look quite promising.  You are leaving no stone unturned.  I am pursuing other angles likewise. <BR> <BR>Ciao, pax56  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2792-->
<!--Post: 2806--><!--Time: 1104160185-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2806"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 7:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Pax <BR> <BR>Merry Christmas and thank you for you enlightening my about the &#34;strange letters&#34;. <BR>You know I´m danish living in Denmark and my english is not near perfect and therfore I´m not always the best to understand texts like those, but I am doing exactly what you said in your post; looking for som kind of track that I also belive that BTK has left in cyberspace, and that could be on pupose or not on purpose IMO. <BR>I´m very happy that you support that kind of work, thanks!, cause most people prefere more specific evidence and often find my way of working the case to far fetched. <BR> <BR>Lokking forward to read more of your posts... <BR> <BR>hugs...skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2806-->
<!--Post: 3026--><!--Time: 1104375137-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3026"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I dont know how you found these Skov.  These are some of the weirdes letters I have ever seen.  In reading them it looks as if they may be part of text commands for a computer game/program.   <BR> <BR>Open the first picture in the second horizontal row and maximize it.  Now look down in the bottom right hand corner.  It says &#34;Can&#39;t bring Sants Rosa Empire Juniors Peal 165&#34; &#40;or 163&#41;followed by a phone number.  I did a google on it and it comes to what looks like a California locale.   <BR> <BR>I as well as you probably have no idea what this means.  What Im wondering is, did anyone try to call the number to see where it leads.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3026-->
<!--Post: 3060--><!--Time: 1104397690-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3060"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hmmm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 1:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe one of the notes had a date on it in the 90&#39;s...I looked at them a few days ago, was it 1991?  It seems that they are computer game/ or some other type of game notes along with normal school notes.  It reminded me of when I had friends who played Dungeons and Dragons.  I never played, but I remember the characters seemed real when spoken about.  It seems this person is creating a world with symbols and rules...a game.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3060-->
<!--Post: 3061--><!--Time: 1104399669-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3061"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 1:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, try putting just bdmonkeys into google, if you haven&#39;t already. There is more out there, but I have to tell you, the stuff I&#39;m reading is making me feel that there is not a connection, in part because it&#39;s all stuff that literally sounds like it&#39;s written by someone too young to be BTK. Perhaps even in their 20&#39;s.  <BR> <BR>It&#39;s very easy sometimes to see BTK lurking around every corner, on the &#39;net and off, and sometimes, when you&#39;re travelling something as vast as the internet, a coincidence really is just a coincidence. But I&#39;ll keep studying this, out of respect for your question, so that I might give you a more complete response myself. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3061-->
<!--Post: 3084--><!--Time: 1104441064-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3084"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Gavinelias<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Gavinelias<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 1:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, I sent you a message on the other board about this post and most of what I discovered.  Let me know if you get it. <BR>Thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3084-->
